---
import { getImage } from "astro:assets"
import library from "../../assets/pivo-cloud-library.webp"
import CaseStudyDemo from "../../components/CaseStudyDemo.astro"
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro"

const [small, medium] = await Promise.all([480, 800].map(width => getImage({ src: library, width, format: "webp" })))
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  path="/work/pivo-cloud/"
  title="Pivo Cloud video library and file management with Vue — Jérôme Schaeffer"
  description="Explore Jérôme Schaeffer’s frontend work on Pivo Cloud at 3i. Browse practice and lesson recordings, inspect file details, and manage storage in a sample library."
  heading="Managing riding videos in Pivo Cloud"
  image={library.src}
  imageWidth={library.width}
  imageHeight={library.height}
  srcset={`${small.src} 480w, ${medium.src} 800w, ${library.src} ${library.width}w`}
  sizes="(min-width: 1174px) 1080px, (max-width: 500px) calc(100vw - 40px), 92vw"
  imageAlt="The Cloud Gallery in selection mode, with one stabilized clip selected and a storage meter beside the file grid."
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    A rider looking for yesterday’s canter practice can start with the day of the ride.
    At 3i, I maintain and extend Pivo Cloud, the Vue 3 web app where riders browse their Pivo Track uploads
    and revisit recorded lessons.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    Selecting a practice clip in the portfolio demo. The sidebar shows storage used across both galleries.
   <a class="text-link" href="/assets/pivo-cloud-current.jpg">See the Pivo Cloud production gallery</a>.
  </Fragment>

  <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="finding-a-recording">
    <h2 id="finding-a-recording">Which gallery holds the recording?</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        A practice clip uploaded from Pivo Track goes in Cloud Gallery. A recorded coaching session goes in Lesson
        Gallery. Within each gallery, the newest day comes first, so a rider looking for yesterday’s work can go
        straight to that group.
      </p>
      <p>
        A badge on a clip shows when it has been stabilized or compressed. A file still being validated stays in
        the grid while it waits. Open a ready clip to see its file type, size, and last modified date, then use the
        arrow keys to step through the other clips.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="file-actions">
    <h2 id="file-actions">What can a rider do with a selection?</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        Select one clip and the library offers Share, Download, and Delete. Add a second clip and the rider can
        share or delete the group. Download is a single-file action. Switching galleries clears the selection so
        the next action applies only to files the rider can see.
      </p>
      <p>
        Both galleries draw on the same storage allowance. Deleting clips asks for confirmation and shows how
        many files will be removed. Once confirmed, the storage meter reflects the space those files occupied.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="demo-section" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
    <h2 id="demo-title">Try the sample library</h2>
    <p>
      Open Lesson Gallery and inspect a recording. Then select two clips, delete them, and watch the storage
      meter change. The demo uses sample files and simulates sharing and downloading. Restart restores the library.
    </p>
    <CaseStudyDemo demo="cloud" label="Open library demo" fallback="Enable JavaScript to try the library controls." />
  </section>
</CaseStudyLayout>
